  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run (1 of 6 used): 3 witnesses, 2 names, 3 atoms read.\n\n**Concept body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/interaction/overtakes.lean`):\n```\nrises(drv_position_behind(b, a))  ∧  since(rel_same_direction(a, b; alignment), drv_position_behind(a, b; alignment))\n```\n- **When it holds:** `rises` picks out the one observation where a becomes wholly ahead of b, so the concept holds there and nowhere else.\n- **The earlier condition:** `since` checks that a was behind b at some earlier observation and that the headings stayed aligned at every observation from then up to the recognition. That is the same as the contract's \"last observation at which a was behind b\" condition.\n- **Unknown, not false:** if the recording never shows a behind b and the headings are aligned back to the start, `since` reaches the start of the recording and reports unknown.\n- **Narrowings:** none needed.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/interaction/overtakes.lean`): two cars of 4 m × 2 m in adjacent east-bound lanes, a at 10 m/s and b at 5 m/s, alignment 9/10, 7 observations one second apart.\n- **holds:** a is wholly behind b for the first 4 observations, alongside at the 5th and wholly ahead from the 6th. The scenario is judged only at the 6th observation (5000 ms), where the concept holds.\n- **fails:** a comes alongside and then keeps pace with b to the end, never getting ahead.\n- **blind:** the holds geometry, but from the alongside observation on, b's length is missing and `rel.longitudinal_overlap` is masked. Earlier observations still show a clearly behind b, so the result at 5000 ms is unknown only because of the masked atom. Without that, the start of the recording would also have counted as a cause and the gate would have rejected the witness.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
